tag blockguy_internal;

use_tag skate_math, blockmesh, builder;

import "../skate/math.l8";

import "../blockmesh/blockmesh.l8";

import "../builder/builder.l8";

import "shape.l8";

import "skeleton.l8"

// The block guy: a tall soft red block with a cap, legs that are columns
// under it (thigh, shin and a boot of a foot), and arms that are bars (an
// upper arm, and a forearm ending in a mitt), with real joints: knees and
// elbows that are hinges and bend one way, and hips and shoulders that
// swing every way, each within the limits a person's do.
//
// shape.l8 builds him into a mesh, every vertex of it with the bone it
// moves with (rigid skinning: see guy_build). skeleton.l8 poses him: a
// GuyPose (the body, where each foot is and how it is turned, and the arms'
// angles) is solved, the legs reaching the feet by two-bone IK, into
// GuyJoints (every joint's angle, within its limits), and those into one
// matrix per bone, for a renderer to draw him with in one draw.
//
// A game's own motions (riding, running) are its own: it makes a GuyPose
// of them each frame. What a GuyPose means is set out with its type.
